The '''Ongree''' were an [[Amphibian|amphibious]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Skustell]]. The [[Jedi]] [[Pablo-Jill]] was a member of this species, as were [[Jedi Master]] [[Coleman Kcaj]] and the [[Anklebiter Brigade]] member [[Urk G'lar]].

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:Pablo-Jill-SWFC.png|thumb|left|200px|An Ongree displaying a "beaked" mouth]]
A species of bipedal, amphibian, piscine [[Humanoid]]s, the Ongree had a tall, tapered cranium, with two [[eye]]stalks emerging from either side of the head, and generally had a lipless [[mouth]] in the center of the forehead, above four [[Nose|nostrils]]. This curious, unconventional positioning of their facial attributes often gave the impression that their heads were on upside-down, and could provide an Ongree with a fearsome aspect. A gathering of fleshy tendrils hung below the chin. Ongree had two [[Limb|arms]] and two legs, and had hairless, orange-yellow skin. Their hands had three digits each, including an opposable thumb.<ref name="Alien Archive" />

==History==
Ongree [[Homeworld|hailed]] from the astronomical object [[Skustell]] located within the [[Skustell Cluster]] in the [[Tarabba sector]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]].<ref name="Appendix">{{GalaxyMapAppendix}}</ref> Skustell was represented in the [[Galactic Senate|Imperial Senate]] by delegates from the world<ref name="MOF">''[[Reign of the Empire: The Mask of Fear]]''</ref> by [[19 BBY]].<ref name="MOFdate">{{MOFdate}}</ref> Ongree were present within the wider galaxy by [[382 BBY]].<ref name="CataclysmDate">''[[Star Wars: The High Republic Character Encyclopedia]]'' dates the events of ''The High Republic: Cataclysm'' to [[382 BBY]].</ref>

By [[34 ABY]]<ref name="AlienArchiveJournalDate">{{AlienArchiveJournalDate}}</ref>, a journal featuring an illustration of an Ongree was displayed at the [[Graf Archive]] on [[Orchis 2]]<ref name="Alien Archive" />. The image, created by an [[Unidentified artist|unknown artist]], was later restored and expanded during the [[Graf Archive restoration effort]] under [[Xoddam Lothipp]]’s tenure as [[Deputy Director]] of the archive.<ref name="Alien Archive" /> According to the same journal, many Ongree were considered even-minded individuals who could be found as [[diplomat]]s and [[negotiator]]s throughout [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Alien Archive" /> 
==Ongree in the galaxy==
===High Republic Era===
[[File:Kunpar-standing-2023THRA11.png|thumb|right|200px|The Ongree Kunpar Vasivola]]
In 382 BBY,<ref name="CataclysmDate" /> at an [[Path compound]] on the planet [[Dalna]], an [[Unidentified Ongree Path of the Open Hand member|Ongree]] male was a [[Path of the Open Hand]] member who confronted [[Enya Keen]] with a lit green [[lightsaber]] that he claimed she did not deserve as a Jedi. He taunted her as "trash", spat on the ground, and acted as a decoy while three other Path warriors attacked her with bludgeons and [[blaster]]s. After Enya dodged attacks, he attempted a death blow with the lightsaber but missed, had his knee joint popped by her scissor kick, dropped the weapon while screaming in agony, and cried out when she struck his bulbous eyes.<ref name="Cataclysm">''[[The High Republic: Cataclysm]]''</ref> The Ongree [[Kunpar Vasivola]]<ref name="Midnight Horizon">''[[The High Republic: Midnight Horizon]]''</ref> was a [[Gender|male]]<ref name="Escape from Valo">''[[The High Republic: Escape from Valo]]''</ref> [[Jedi Master]] of the [[Jedi Order]] during the [[High Republic Era]], stationed at the [[Valo Temple]] on the [[planet]] [[Valo]].<ref name="Race to Crashpoint Tower">''[[The High Republic: Race to Crashpoint Tower]]''</ref>

[[Ruusstha Vidyarvrikt]] was an elderly Ongree<ref name="Trail of Shadows 1" /> from Dalna<ref name="Trail of Shadows 3">[[The High Republic: Trail of Shadows 3|''The High Republic: Trail of Shadows'' 3]]</ref> who served the Jedi Order 35 years prior to [[231 BBY]],<ref name="Trail of Shadows 1 Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''The High Republic: Trail of Shadows'' 1 to [[231 BBY]].</ref> and often sang a nursery rhyme to Jedi younglings, including [[Emerick Caphtor]] and [[Stellan Gios]]. Emerick speculated that the song was intended to terrify the younglings into behaving.<ref name="Trail of Shadows 1">[[The High Republic: Trail of Shadows 1|''The High Republic: Trail of Shadows'' 1]]</ref> In [[230 BBY]],<ref name="Date note">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''The High Republic: The Battle for Starlight'' to [[230 BBY]].</ref> one Ongree tried to flee [[Eiram]] due to the groundquakes and storms on the planet when Jedi arrived to help the fleeing citizens. A Ongree  worker with a clipboard also helped citizens flee. <ref name="Battle for Starlight">''[[The High Republic: The Battle for Starlight]]''</ref> By [[228 BBY]],<ref name="228 BBY Date">{{THRContent228BBY|DFS}}</ref> an Ongree crew member was assisted by [[Jordanna Sparkburn]] in unloading containers of protein and laser parts, during which the physical labor helped channel her stress.<ref name="Defy the Storm">''[[The High Republic: Defy the Storm]]''</ref>

===Clone Wars===
[[Pablo-Jill]] was an Ongree became a Jedi Knight<ref name="Alien Archive" /> prior to the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="AOTC" /> He<ref name="Force Collection">{{ForceCollection|Pablo-Jill|star=3}}</ref> fought in [[First Battle of Geonosis]], jumping into the [[Petranaki Arena]] to enter combat with other Jedi.<ref name="AOTC" /> The Ongree [[Coleman Kcaj]] also served in the Jedi Order, attaining the rank of Master and sitting on the [[Jedi High Council]].<ref name="Alien Archive" />

===Imperial Era===
[[File:Ongree-fan-BV1.jpg|thumb|left|180px|An Ongree fan of the podracer Sebulba]]
Around [[10 BBY]],<ref name="BeyondVictoryDate">{{BeyondVictoryDate|comic=1}}</ref> in a bar in the [[Galma]] outskirts, a male Ongree approached the [[Podracer (profession)|podracer]] [[Sebulba]] for an autograph, but the [[Dug]] kicked the Ongree into a waiter who was carrying multiple beverages, spilling them over [[Bossk'wassak'Cradossk|Bossk]] and causing a brawl.<ref name="Beyond Victory 1">''Beyond Victory'' 1</ref> 

The Ongree [[Urk G'lar]] joined the [[Anklebiter Brigade]], a group of children led by the [[human]] [[Iggs]] who were rebelling against the Empire on G'lar's [[homeworld]] [[Coruscant]]. G'lar was one of six members of the brigade who infiltrated the [[Imperial Palace]] to [[assassin]]ate [[Grand Vizier]] [[Mas Amedda]]. Amedda offered a bargain, that if the children could liberate him from the palace by eliminating the guards outside his chamber, he would yield the Empire to the [[New Republic]]. G'lar and the group accepted and successfully rescued Amedda, and he honored his promise by representing the Empire at the signing of the [[Galactic Concordance]] peace treaty.<ref name="Empire's End">''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]''</ref>

===New Republic Era===
[[File:Skeleton-crew-lanupa-Ongree.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Ongree relaxing in the Mud Pits]]
Around [[9 ABY]],<ref name="SC Date">{{SkeletonCrewDate}}</ref> at least two Ongree were present on the planet [[Lanupa]] when the ''[[Onyx Cinder]]'', piloted by the [[Skeleton Crew]], undertook a [[Mission to Skull Ridge Mountain|mission]] to [[Skull Ridge Mountain]]. These Ongree bathed in the [[Mud Pits]] at the [[Skull Ridge Mountain Hotel & Spa]].<ref name="Learn About Pirates">{{SkeletonCrew|You Have a Lot to Learn About Pirates}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The Ongree were first developed as the species for the character of Pablo Jill in [[2002]] film [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']], directed by [[George Lucas]].<ref name="AOTC" /> Ongree were never identified on-screen but were named in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] book ''[[Star Wars Chronicles: The Prequels]]'', from 2005, by written by [[Stephen J. Sansweet]] and [[Pablo Hidalgo]].<ref name="SWCTP">''[[Star Wars Chronicles: The Prequels]]''</ref> Ongree were first identified in the rebooted [[Canon]] continuity in the [[2017]] book ''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]'' written by [[Chuck Wendig]].<ref name="Empire's End" /> Ongree were represented, through the character Coleman Kcaj, in the noncanonical Minecraft tie-in ''[[Minecraft Star Wars: Path of the Jedi]]''.<ref name="Minecraft">''[[Minecraft Star Wars: Path of the Jedi]]''</ref>

